  "source_description": "IsValidDLCID calls DLCID.GetDLCID and uses two ceq instructions to return a value indicating whether the mapped integer is not -1. IsOwner calls IsValidDLCID, passes that return value to the Steamworks.AppId_t constructor MemberRef, then invokes Steamworks.SteamApps.BIsSubscribedApp. Its original catch clause is System.Object covering IL+15..+29 only; when a catch occurs, the method sets its return local to zero. The AppId_t constructor is before the guarded region. These are exact code paths; no Steam ownership or valid app ID is established.",
  "limits": [
    "Method and IL/source metadata prove original call and catch control flow but do not establish whether Steamworks initializes, which account is logged in, or whether BIsSubscribedApp succeeds.",
    "The original source passes the result of IsValidDLCID into AppId_t. Do not infer that this is the mapped integer app-ID or correct an apparent surprising conversion.",
    "The original catch System.Object covers the IL interval [15,29); it does not cover the AppId_t constructor or the validity-helper call before that interval.",
    "DLCID.GetDLCID is pinned to an exact original 143-byte method and SHA for direct callee identity; its switch table and actual integer mapping have not been promoted as authored runtime facts here.",
    "Direct callers are limited to two explicitly audited original functions; actual DLC ownership, installed game data, and complete calling context remain unverified.",
